## AFTER MOVEMENT 9 — chapters 54–60, days 306–308 (drafted 2026-10-12, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)

### Coordinator rulings (binding) — the book's exit state is in "State at movement end" below and in plan-audit.md §8
- **Entry seam with Movement 8 ratified** (Sol plan audit): first light on the 306th at the shale camp; twelve and a mule; thirteen fragments; deployment thirty-three; purse 123; Vastin day twenty-seven; Teague's arm on a slat; the broad man on a stick; Oryn six days past her cairn and untold of the thirteenth.
- **The pass (the 306th).** Seln went in through the pool at the mouth by night: a gap a hundred strides long and eight wide; a sheer wall on the right hand going in (south); on the left (north) a bank of loose shale up to a shelf with **nine, perhaps ten, and three bows** (the Span's seven among them, by a cough), **two heaps of stone on timber frames, each held by one wedge**, a dead pine roped to the first, and a stair of broken rock at the far end; the team's own path comes in over the ridge. Protected: "It's through." (**Cael**, over his drawing). Brom: a wall cannot hold a hill, but "You lean it."
- **THE WALL, SITTING.** Nobody asked Vastin. He asked **Oryn** whether she would amend her term ("If you will not, I shall not do the thing"); she read the knee, asked first ("Yes"), and allowed it only seated, the leg laid out, "not a pound of you on it", warning that it would spend him and that she could not give that back. **Minted, bounded: an Iron Wall can be raised through whatever its holder has set upon the ground; it still cannot be moved while it stands.** The doctrine was told once to Teague's four — protected: "Behind it. Noted?" (Cael) / "Noted," (**Teague's boy**, with his whole head). **The tall man spoke to the six for the first time: "And then?"** — Cael: "Then I don't know."
- **The seven flights.** (1) Brom, both hands full setting the old man down, took a bolt through the LEFT forearm before he could go to Iron. (2) The wall went up as a lean-to slant from the stones behind Vastin's back to a high edge on the hill. (3) Three bolts at Vastin broke on it. (4) **The maul: the first heap, the pine and the whole bank came down the plane and shut the western mouth behind them**; nothing came through; the bank was left a bare slab ("the quilt off the table"), and Seln went up it. (5) The broad man went to the shelter's edge to draw the bows and was hit in the RIGHT shoulder, falling half outside. (6) **Teague's boy went out a stride at the hurt man's look — no order — and was killed.** Lira was twenty strides back at the low end, where the field had put her; the tall man's hand closed on air. Oryn asked "May I?", waited a breath for an answer that could not come, and went in without; her hands came off with nothing done — **her first death under her hands**. **The broad man said the boy's name once; the page does not render it and Cael will not write it (OWNER #54 default).** (7) Brom stood out to draw the seventh while Seln came over the lip.
- **THE THIRTEENTH, USED.** Cael told Teague only "something that nobody'll hear … it's not mine alone to tell", went up the slab on his hands, set heel and palm and **let it go once (*Yes.*) on the second heap's western upright: the frame and its cartload went a body's length ALONG the shelf into the team's own hollow; not one stone went over; nobody stood on the line.** The cost came back to the old three ribs: **two cracked along the old line, the third sore.** **Deployment thirty-four.** Teague was on the stair with his face to the rock; he saw a heap where a rig had stood and a boy holding his side, "knows the look of a bill", and did not ask. **He is still untold.**
- **The breaking.** Teague came up the stair left-handed; **the tall man reversed his spear and carried the butt foremost**; nine went east by the cleft and along the ridge, none struck, none taken, no face seen; Seln had one in his cord and did not lift the cloth. Seln: "Nine." Vastin let the wall go at Lira's word and went over on his side; Karis sat by him with her bound hand on his shoulder. Protected, Teague's, kneeling by his dead, to Cael: **"A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't."** At the eastern mouth Cael understood what the line he had followed was drawn in: "It was not ink."
- **Burial and the plain's edge.** Teague's crew buried the boy at the eastern mouth in their own order (the older healer washed his face with his own cloth; the tall man laid the bed; the broad man set the first stone; Teague the last); the six carried stone at his leave ("Carry.") and laid none. **Eleven.** Teague began a figure and did not say it. Lira and Seln fetched the mule by the ridge path; Seln's finding: at the fence they had been told to hold and to see; here somebody had been told to stop a crew. That night the tall man wrung out a cloth for Teague's arm in the boy's place.
- **Oryn and the thirteenth.** "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." / "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." (protected). She knew it for Teague's make and was told how it came. **Oryn now knows the thirteenth; Teague and Vastin do not.** "No term tonight." She will carry nobody's account to another. (Cutaway: she set no term because she will not set one out of fright; she has not heard the leaf; the older healer laid a hot cloth over her hands.)
- **The instruments (the 306th night),** by lamp, in Cael's hand only: **the cord a stride short in forty-two; the Ternhall edge a hair and a half out; Hesk's, two.** True in Karis's hand and Brom's. "Cause: not found. No inference entered." The trend is up; no line is drawn. His Arbiter is dark and unchanged.
- **THE STILL PLACE, READ AS MADE.** Having gone over Cleon's warning and whose leave he had, he turned the twelfth inward **on purpose**: *Still.* / *Set.* / *Bones.* / a floor with nothing built on it / an instruction with no language. Protected: "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." **He told no one — not Oryn, not Karis, not Lira.** The S22 log (protected, whole, once) is in his book; **he held the book out to Lira and asked her not to read that entry until after the morrow, and she pushed it back unread** ("I don't read ahead."). Not counted as a deployment (a reading of himself, as the five with the tenth were not).
- **The court (the 307th).** Cael's own lowercase word, from a great house seen at Ostrand. It lies LOW: worn rock runs in to **a cut two fingers wide**, and inside it a floor of the grey, level and bare, that keeps the light; **eleven stumps** inside the rim (the Fallow has eleven); courses of writing between the cut and the bare middle; eight rusted peg-holes outside ("This they have only pegged"); no registry iron. **Corded round, by Lira heel-to-toe on the lip with Seln, Karis calling and Cael tallying without touching the hemp: 158 lengths and 19 strides (3,179 strides); about fifty lengths across — about 1,107 yards; 506 strides from the cut to the middle; round to a nail's breadth.** Vastin, on a box at the first stump, was the mark the round closed on. Karis: one cutting lies under all four that she had — a slip of the tool here is COPIED on a sheet from the Hall and on one from the Span's pier: "The others are copies." The thumbnail ring was inked; **the Ternhall brass and Hesk's strip met square on the line ("both edges")**; "*No sixth found.*" The council: Cael's three sentences again and one more ("And if they're on that plain, they're let off it."); Teague: "It stands." The nine's marks go south.
- **At the line (dusk).** One at a time, asked first, Oryn's fingers on each wrist: Lira "Right."; Brom priced a stump ("something's had this down to a stool"); Karis "It's the first one."; Seln's count — as at the four. **Vastin** (protected): "I stood at a line for forty years … and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." **Oryn** (protected): "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." — unanswered. **Teague** stepped over for the first time and back (protected): "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." — and turned his three to the west. The close (protected, Lira / Cael): "Every other one, yours worked and ours died." / "Yes." / "You think this one's different." / "I think this one's the first one they made … it's the one they built to make sure I'd never be." / He stepped over the line. / His Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have. / "Wait here,".
- **THE CENTRE.** He walked alone. **At a hundred strides he turned the twelfth on the floor, on purpose: the same reading** — *Still. Set. Bones.*; something that bears, with nothing carried on it; a lean with no letter. **Deployment thirty-five.** At five hundred and six there was nothing to see. What he had always known in himself by everything that parted on it had **no edge and no seam** there: "Not the Quiet." / "Not a fragment." / "The same kind of made." (protected, spoken aloud to nobody). "Here the foot arrived." **He fit. It was not an accident. He does not know what it is instead; the step beyond was left lying.** He counted five hundred and six back.
- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." / "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road," … "If there's road." He gave the others the count and "Nothing happened. Nothing went, of mine." "Twenty-nine tomorrow," (Vastin) / "Thirty's the month," (Oryn). (Cutaway: Vastin at the rim, a man still there when the thing beside his face had gone; **he does not mean to ask them anything**; the sentence about a man and an apparatus set down unfinished; Brom: "You're relieved.")
- **The ledger and the letter (the 307th night), protected, each once:** "Thirteen: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. One anomaly, the still place, read by two instruments … Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made. That is as far as the instruments go and I am not going past them." / "Stood in the middle of the first one. Nothing. Entered." Owed otherwise, side by side: to Vastin the eleventh, to Teague the thirteenth; "A debt is not paid by something that the creditor is not let to know." The letter to Hesk: "Nineteen. Your grandmother's line was already drawn. I followed it to the end; both edges agreed. Tell Lira's family I said so. Mind the shape, you said. I'm minding it. — C." (OWNER #55: verbatim, no setup.)
- **The dawn (the 308th).** Teague took the letter for Pike's hand; protected: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," (Cael) / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." He did not say the number of his own; **four went west ahead: the tall man, the broad man, the older healer, and Teague last.** The broad man to Vastin: "Aye." Oryn read each of them, asked first (Karis's palm: "It'll leave a line."; Vastin's knee "a day from done"); protected: "The day I have to." (when she will hear the leaf) / "Noted," (Cael) / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." **She rode the mule north toward the salt road and three holds, eight days past her cairn; she has still not heard the leaf.** Vastin took up the tarred case and stood a stride behind Brom; **he asked for no place and was offered none.** Seln (protected): "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." — **the six on that rock are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin; it is a count, not an admission** (it is not the six of the ferry town, of whom Oryn was one). "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. **The closing prose stands whole, once, last.**
- **Final counts.** Thirteen fragments; **deployment since the Line thirty-five**; purse **123** (nothing spent in the movement); Vastin day twenty-nine of thirty on the 308th; Karis carries sixty-one sheets and the hide with five rings and a line; one dead, unnamed, under a cairn at the pass's eastern mouth. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 36,600 against 36,000.
- **Left open on purpose:** the third sentence; what Cael is; Vastin's place; Teague's and Vastin's debts; the leaf and the lamps page unjoined; the two seals; the deep-layer date; the chronicle's hole; the instruments' trend; Seln's case; the faceless nine; Oryn's hearing of the leaf; "Tell Lira's family I said so".

