    72	
    73	He climbed beside Teague's posts and did it again at two hundred yards, and again at sixty, a long way beyond her, where he could see the lichen on the nearest animal's plates. At sixty the read told him nothing whatever about the herd, since its whole world was a pace and a half across. It told him about the slope under his boots. He shut it, and looked back along the hill.
