   101	"Then that's three hours' mowing, and four people who can hold a shovel."
   102	
   103	She had worked that out from a sledge, with one arm tied and a bow that she could not bend, while four people with two good hands apiece stood round a page; he had been reading the ground, and she had been reading the only thing on that hill that could kill them.
   104	
   105	Brom had been looking along the slope with one eye shut.
   106	
   107	"It wants to climb," he said. "Your strip. If it runs level they'll finish it level, and they'll be standing on my last six holes when they've done. A hand in the yard, the whole way. I'll walk it out."
