editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-007/plan-audit-prompt.md-33-- **The grade.** Three marks; the first-tier box ruled and never used; **no first-tier site appears**; ages by first sheet 61, 94, 138, 206 (which site is which, against Movements 1–5's sheets: the Ring 11, the Stair 29, the Hall 12, the Fallow?); the third-tier point past the fourth, in the straightedge's shadow; oldest-last; "It's observation … Not what it means." **The log, verbatim (Tier C S17 log)** — the grandmother is Cael's (§12 C4); "after the thaw" stands as printed in the plan; "four hundred years ago" stands here only. Is the log printed whole and once?
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-007/plan-audit-prompt.md:34:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." Two healers (Oryn; Teague's — unnamed). Vastin ordered to stand; his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn's terms ("three holds owed"; "a stop on my own route"; "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."). **Consent explicit at every reading ("May I?")**: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm; Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut" — is Oryn told that Vastin put a Wall on it against her order, as he asked that she be told?). **The deep reading:** "May I?" / "Yes."; her current goes ROUND the place; the twelfth turns inward unbidden (*still*, then *set*), is not named, shows in neither his wrist nor his face; the eyes pay in the dark; **Oryn's finding verbatim (Tier A 25)**; Cael withholds his own and enters his reasons in order; **what is Oryn told at Millrace of the two tellings Cael owes her** (the self-readings "round the place"; the twelfth)? The packet says the Rune finding is told to NO ONE — distinguish the finding (*still* / *set*) from the fact of the twelfth, and state what the page does. Lira offers the leaf; Oryn does NOT hear it ("Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-007/plan-audit-prompt.md-35-- **Dawn (299th).** "Twelve and a mule": name the twelve by role and check the wall's count (ten) against them. The pencil line from the fourth circle onto the blank sheet and past the divider's point — Hesk's dividers were "never opened on a distance" through Movement 6 (Cael's ruling of the 168th): are they opened here, by whom, on whose leave (Karis asked for the loan of them; "Teague is at the door for the dividers, not the marks")?
