editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-H-RERUN.md:10:Book 7 now closes on the **hundred and thirty-first morning**, at the lower inn hearth in Lowmarch, after the carter brings Oryn's letter through a hand's depth of snow. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130. Book 8's day-131 opening therefore stands and its relative day spine does **not** shift, but its opening must be placed after the Book 7 hearth scene, not while the ferryman is still taking in the ropes (`chapter-59.md:3,47–49,121–147`; `chapter-60.md:47–95,219–265`).
