+- **Ch37.** First scene: `The bridge was a made thing` … `if you know how that's done."` Last scene: `The floor was of beaten clay,` … `went to see to the mule.` Day 292. Karis reaches all twenty-three letters without guessing. Hesk's dividers remain unused under Cael's standing instrument ruling. Three unbidden outward twelfth readings (`bears`, then `bears/nothing`) cost the eyes and remain undeployed. Seln closes his case without naming its contents. Cael's inventory cleanly distinguishes twelve fragments, five tenth/self-readings and thirty-two deployments. Lira is twenty-seven days out of wool. Oryn's first death is brief, preceded by consent work and carried as a real cost.
