editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md:221:"Nothing is mine that I have not counted." She drew the gloves on, a finger at a time, and slipped the tape of the uppermost row, and turned back its first sheet by the edges.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md:231:Four signs stood at the head of the dead man's page, and after them the number thirty-two.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-08.md:237:The third was a boy with a tally stick, on the western landing, on the evening of the twelfth day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-09.md:265:*Two hundred and seventy-seventh day. The read: the ground, at the landing, from the post's foot to the old sill. In earnest. Deployment since the Line: thirty.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-07.md:199:He wrote nine more, and said them; and then he stopped, with the brush lifted, and looked at the eleventh line of the old cloth, and at the ledger under its stone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-07.md:205:"You're nothing of the kind. I can't carry a number that I never wrote. So I carry the place." The brush came down, and five names went onto clean canvas in the square black hand, one after another, on the eleventh line. "Eleventh. I'll not have it said that I moved a crew up or down a cloth for want of knowing where to put it. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-07.md:213:"Eleventh," he said, to nobody, and went to fetch the pails.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-12.md:301:*Deployment since the Line: thirty.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:49:Cael had Hesk's book inside his coat, and he did not need to take it out, since every figure in it had stopped at this river. There were nine lines under five names in a one-armed man's ledger, and a sheet of sailcloth by the inn's hearth with those names on its eleventh line, and neither would change by a stroke while the holds were shut. There were ninety-six marks in a purse. There were twenty-seven uses written against the ten fragments.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:61:In the west each of them had been a line in a registry: an Ember of the third rank in Iron, and a Wind of the first; an Iron Skin who had stopped at Copper and said so without shame; and a Shadow, Bronze, whom fifteen years of service had taught to be overlooked. Nobody out here had asked any of them for a tier since the ninth day. The board at the foot of the meadow priced the job and never the person. By its reckoning the five of them stood eleventh among the crews on a sheet of sailcloth, which was all the rank that this country kept.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:65:It was registry iron, a foot and a half long. It had a number struck into its head, thirty-two, and beneath the number a short stroke and a bar. Its point had been turned on a wheel, and it was bright.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:223:The keeper said, "Pike," and Pike said, "Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:281:*Hundred and thirty-third day. Lowmarch, the lower inn. The cold stay is paid: four a month, five months, twenty in front. In hand, seventy-six. The reserve is not counted here. Nine lines, and no number against the season, on purpose. Eleventh on the cloth. The board has a roof, a well-house and a fence. The fence is ours, and we go out to it on the hundred and thirty-eighth. The roof is ours as well, at five, paid when it has kept a thaw out. The mule stands in the ferryman's shed, at a fee he has not asked for and will.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:285:*The ten, by use. Trials, in the ferryman's shed, at night, with the door kept. Not uses. Not counted.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:293:*Deployment since the Line: twenty-seven.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-03.md:17:He let that lie where he had put it. Cael saw what it had cost him to bring such a thing down a hill and say it in another crew's corner. He was first on a sailcloth sheet, and he had just priced his own people at nothing in front of the eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-03.md:293:*Hundred and fiftieth day. The shed. Trials. Not counted.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-03.md:305:*Deployment since the Line: twenty-eight.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-34.md:13:*This far?* said the eleventh, of the ladder's head, where a line might have been set that nobody could have climbed past.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-34.md:99:The eleventh had asked at that slot. *This far?* It had asked in the voice of a bar going home into two sockets; and it had been quite right, since that was exactly what the place was for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-34.md:233:The eleventh had nothing to do in that gallery, and it did it all day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-02.md:229:"It's a use," said Cael. "It's the first since the marsh. Deployment since the Line, twenty-eight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:243:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two. Myself, twice: not counted, as before.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md:243:*Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md:263:"I have left this for thirty-four days," she said. "I did not wish to read another person's findings until I had finished entering my own. I have finished."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md:269:"He begins with this. Four signs in a row, and after them the number, thirty-two. It is how he names the place that he is standing in." Her finger did not move. "They are a clerk's signs. They are not a carver's; I have forty-one kinds of mark from three floors, and these are not cut like any of them. Seln read registry paper for fifteen years, and he does not know the index that they are taken from."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-05.md:171:She knew that mark from four places. It was struck into the head of the stake in that case, and into the newer of two iron bars at a grey stone on the Stair road; it was on every bar of a fence round a place that she had not been let into, under the number thirty-four; and it was here. It stood beside the Stair twice over and beside the fourth place, and she had never found it beside the Fallow or the hall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-05.md:215:*That is the ten. Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-24.md:269:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:77:He had said it to the peats, and everybody at that fire turned to him, since he did not give figures that he had not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:277:He had a good deal to carry besides the box, and he went over it, a stride at a time, as he would have gone over a count. There was a job, done and paid, with a hundred and thirty-eight marks to show for it. There was a wall that he had stood behind for the space of one count, and an eleventh thing that had not come of it. There was a mark in a small ruled square, which was on four sheets and an iron stake and which nobody could read. He had a name, short and strange, for a man who sat under a town. He had two sentences in a book, in his own hand, about a flight of steps and a paved place.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-32.md:257:*No*, he told it; and that was the eleventh time, in that stair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:67:It was the twelfth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:139:"Twelfth. His. Lean."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:211:"There's a twelfth. It came an hour ago, at the fifth row, when your finger stopped. It's a piece of yours. I can see which way a run goes. I looked at that row, and at your board, and I've looked at nothing since."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:297:*Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md:265:*Deployment since the Line: thirty.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:35:"The eleventh's the old man's. It came in a stair, under the town, while he held a wall for us on that knee, and he doesn't know. I can't tell him how it came without telling him how all of them came, and that's six people's to give."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:41:"And the twelfth?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:135:It was at about the three hundredth breath that the twelfth turned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:137:He had not bidden it, or so much as thought of it, since he had been counting, and the count was all of him that was awake. The twelfth had lain where she said, a little flat thing behind his eyes, folded; for seven days it had leaned at whatever a hand had made, at pegs and rivets and the piers of a bridge, and each time he had given his eyes some other work, and it had come up short.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:141:And something was being drawn in him, under her hands, which had never been drawn before. It was an outline. Her current went round the place on every side, and round again; and the twelfth came about to that, mildly, as a head comes round in a dark room toward the only sound in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:149:The twelfth leaned, for the space of three breaths, at the middle of him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:153:There was no voice in it; it was only there, as the weight of a stone is there in the hand that lifts it. It was not *nothing*. He knew how the twelfth said that: flatly, of a red square of tile, or of a table's idle leg. It was not *sits*, which it said of a page. It was a word that he had never had of it before; and he had used that very word himself, in a log, for longer than he had owned the thing which now said it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:165:*Set*: as a stone is set, or a stake. He knew three places where he had met that word. The eleventh had come into him in a stair, not as a filling, but as a post is stood in its hole; a small pale woman had found the word under her own glove, when she had wished for a name; and it stood in the fourth line of a list on the back of a skin, hung level with the people at a kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:247:It ran for a long time. He had not turned the twelfth; it had turned of itself, and he had not looked at anything, with his eyes or without them. It billed him all the same, to the grain, as a toll-keeper charges a cart that was pushed through his gate by somebody else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:275:*Two hundred and ninety-eighth day, night. Millrace; the cart-shed. A hundred and twenty-seven. Told Oryn, before she read me: the two readings at the brook and the post, and why; the eleventh; the twelfth. Then she read me, asked first, for forty minutes, as deep as she goes. Her finding is hers. I have it word for word, and I am not copying it here, since she can say it.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-46.md:287:*Ruling: hold. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:145:Nobody answered him. Cael had heard those words given, on a frozen road, by a square woman with her sleeves pushed up: that a man who stood a wall on that leg inside the month would keep the stick for the rest of his days. It was the eleventh day of thirty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:155:*Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:283:*Two hundred and ninetieth day; Treswick; the loft; a hundred and thirty-four. The cut, at dusk: six, hooded, two from the yard and four from the lane, with staves, one bow and one dark lantern, and no Path opened by any of them. Nobody dead, none taken, no faces. Karis: the left palm, on a step's edge; seven stitches, Brom's; no healer, since a healer here wants a name. Brom: both shoulders. Lira: the right shoulder, on a wall, and the arm did not take it. V.: a wall, on the eleventh day of thirty; the knee has gone again, and he cannot hold a bowl.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:289:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:293:*Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. Since my Kindling I've learned to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:307:*This far?* said the eleventh, of the dark.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-16.md:215:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-42.md:133:*This far?* said the eleventh, of the three-mile post.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-42.md:147:That was the weight of the morning, and it was all in those two yards. He had entered a wall once, at this man's asking, and had entered more than was asked for. He could not pay it. A thing of that kind could not be told by itself; whoever heard how the eleventh had come would have heard how all of them came, and that was not Cael's to hand over. It belonged to four others who walked in front of the dray, and to a healer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-42.md:291:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-17.md:83:She drew that one out. It was from the fourth row, and it had the Stair's signs at its head, and the number thirty-two. At its foot, in the ruled space, there were four words. They were not in any of the three clerks' hands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-27.md:285:He had been in a great many buildings since he was fourteen, and in every one of them there had been a drawer. There was a counter at Denvash, with a pen on it. There was a house on a bluff, where a file had grown as thick as a man's hand; there was a district seat, and a borrowed office. He had learned to feel for the drawer on any threshold, as a dog feels for the one board in a floor that gives. Even on the kind side of the Line there had been a book, kept by a man with one arm; that one had been honest, and he had been glad to stand in it, and it had put him eleventh all the same.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:15:*Two hundred and ninety-first day. Treswick; the loft; one in the stall. A hundred and thirty-four. By the carts' street, both ways, on wheels: a weight chalked at the bottom gate to the name on the card, and to nobody else. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:17:He ruled a line, and wrote the twelfth's lines under it, in their order, as he had got them by heart on a stair, and added the two that were his.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:27:*Twelfth. Rune, from the reader, at his own table, while he showed Karis how a row goes. Told: Lira first; then him. He is the first outside the six who has it from my mouth how one came. Brom and Karis and Lira gave their word for it on the stair. S. and Oryn to be told. V. is not told, and I have now said to a stranger what I could not say to the man it's owed to. That's heavier than it was this morning. It stands.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:45:"You have a twelfth," he said. "And you have told a registered practitioner of the Compact, beneath its oldest registry, how you came by it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:219:*This far?* said the eleventh, of the shed's mouth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:343:*No*, he told the eleventh; and he turned his back on a brazier, and went down the street.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:375:*Night of the 291st. Followed the boots, with S., round the whole of the lower town. All of them asked; Shadow asked for three hours. One look that I didn't mean, with the twelfth, at the rope-walk: a grain in each eye. Not counted. Nothing opened.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:379:*S.: they have time. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:51:The book came down from the eleventh shelf of the eastern gallery, on the two hundred and eighty-eighth day, in a girl's right hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:263:"A hundred and thirty-four," he said, to the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-58.md:227:*Nobody has crossed. Deployment since the Line: thirty-four.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:287:*Two hundred and eighty-fifth day. Treswick; the loft. A hundred and thirty-six. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two. Lamp, from about the third hour. He says left and I go left.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-45.md:37:She drew the iron out. It was a stake as long as her forearm, numbered thirty-two, with its point still bright, since nobody had ever driven it; and she laid its head under the window, beside the first page of a dead man's book and the corner of an office's sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-45.md:229:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-45.md:391:"Yes." He let himself down. "There is a thing which you must have first. I asked that you be told it, eight days ago, and I find that I had rather tell you. I stood a wall upon that leg on the eleventh day, and I had your words in my head as the stick came down. I heard them, and I did it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-44.md:13:He had been home from the shoulder hold for a week. He had taken that salt up himself, behind the first carts, when he might have sent it with the bow and saved his own boots; the bow had said so, and had been right. But a cut that had eaten three carts in one cold term had been opened in an afternoon by the eleventh crew on Pike's cloth, and Teague had wished to see the ground.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-44.md:151:"That's when I left off looking," he said. "It's not a number. It says that on this day the keeper of this book knew what he didn't know, and signed for it." He blotted the place with the heel of his hand. "Eleventh. And dated."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-44.md:213:He nodded, by the width of a finger, and it was done, and he had not offered his hand. There was a cloth on a nail behind Pike's head with one name alone on its first line and five in a row on its eleventh; and a contract did not take either of them down. Cael found that he did not wish it to. He would sooner walk east beside a man who was ten places better at a thing, and said so, than beside a friend who had to be reminded which of them the ledger preferred.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-44.md:217:*Two hundred and ninety-seventh day. Lowmarch; the hearth's end, and one on the keeper's settle. Eleven miles, and the ferry. The rope is paid: sixty yards of four, and he would take no fare. Pike has twelve lines, and a thirteenth with nothing in its last two columns. He has put a day against the season. A hundred and twenty-eight. Vastin: eighteen of thirty.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-44.md:223:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-47.md:41:She had set it there herself, on the hundred and thirteenth day: a grey thing as big as a loaf, picked out of the rut, to mark the stride at which her own sigil went out. It had lain there through a siege and a morning's measuring. It was not there now. In its place the turf was whole; and Cael, coming down to it behind her, saw why. A square had been cut, with a spade, and lifted, and laid back upon the hollow where a stone had bedded itself.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-47.md:109:He went at it then as he went at a page. A crossbow had been spanned on that brow eleven times, and a twelfth half done; he had heard the count from a stair. A man who spans puts his boot in an iron and hauls, and he would not do that on a slope, or in soft turf, where the stirrup sank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-47.md:193:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-47.md:285:The twelfth leaned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-47.md:307:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-48.md:105:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-48.md:327:*Thirty-two, and that one. Deployment since the Line: thirty-three.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:79:"I've seen that go up a bank," he said. "A fortnight since, at the western landing, with a box on it; and a tall girl, and a little one with a roll of hide. You're off the one-armed man's cloth. The eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:111:*Bears*, said the twelfth, of the rivet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:211:He had not meant to make the inventory that night. He made one at the start of a thing; and he could not have said, climbing the ladder, what was starting. But he had a twelfth, which was not yet in any count. He had a pair of brass legs in his coat from a man who had taught him to write the count first. And there was a bundle on a shelf, two hundred yards over his head, which a pair of square pale fingers would untie in the morning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:217:*Treswick; the loft over the stable; one in the stall. The two hundred and ninety-second day. Eight days inside. A hundred and thirty: four to a dinner, on Brom's ruling, and worth it. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-29.md:311:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:47:Three nights ago, in a stair, six people had come to see what that boy was; and he had stood upon a step with his stick, on the eleventh day of thirty, and put a wall in front of him. He had not known then what stood behind it. He had said so, on a pallet, when he could not hold a bowl. He knew a little more this afternoon. He found that he would do it again, knowing; and that in a day which had taken the floor out from under forty years, it was the single act of his that he could look at without wishing to revise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-53.md:139:"I thought so. I'd only wanted it said." He looked at the slab, and at a doorsill of rock. "And she says there's a thirteenth, and whose. He put his arm through a wall for us. You've come away with the trick of it, and he's sat there thanking you for a stick."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-53.md:149:"As a trial. Not counted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-53.md:269:*The thirteenth: lined, on a slab, behind the step. Not let go. The ribs would take it. A trial; not counted. Thirteen. Deployment since the Line: thirty-three.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-43.md:107:*This far?* said the eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-43.md:199:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-50.md:133:*Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact: from the ground, through the man, out at the hand, and nothing to either side of the line. Needs a thing to push against — the barricade, the ground under the feet; nothing at a distance; nothing from the air. A body's length. The cost back along the same line, every time, at the place the line comes out. Engagement field: close; braced. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Thirteenth.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-50.md:167:"Thirty-four," she said. "A body can stand on it. I have stood on three such, and so have three others here. What you carry will not stand there with you; it goes at the stride. And I told you behind a brow that I cannot say whether a place of this measure gives it back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-50.md:191:Three people on that shelf knew why. The rest saw a boy with a stick step over a bar of iron numbered thirty-four, two strides onto the turf, and turn round. Under his breastbone the thin note had asked at the bar, and the post in him had asked at the line. He had told them no. Nothing else in him so much as blinked: there were twelve things going round a still one, as they went on any ground, and a thirteenth that was not yet a minute old.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-40.md:277:*Two hundred and ninety-third day. Treswick; the yard, and then the loft; one in the stall. A hundred and thirty. A leaf read once, below, by Karis. A copy made. Read at a fire by the three who had not heard it. The reader came up, and ate half a bowl. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-57.md:249:*The thirteenth is used. Once: on the frame of the second heap, along the shelf, at nobody. It came back to the three ribs, where I said that it would. Oryn has been told whose it was. Teague has not.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-57.md:253:*Turned the Rune fragment on myself. Cleon said don't. The reading only ever told me the still place was nothing — no flow, no current, a hole where a man should have a middle. The Rune sense says it's not a hole. It says it's* built like something *— like one of those floors with nothing standing on it. Same shape to that fragment as the sites are to Cleon's. I'm not going to write what that might mean, because I don't know, and because the last time I wrote something true in this log a healer made me swear an oath about it. The instruments read wronger for me than they did at Lowmarch. The trend's climbing. My Arbiter's still dark—nothing in me to go quiet, same as always. Tomorrow, the oldest one. I've spent the whole year wanting to stand in the middle of it. I think part of me already knows what I'm going to feel. Nothing. I think I'm going to feel nothing, and I think that's going to be the loudest thing that's ever happened to me.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-57.md:257:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-three, and the frame this morning: thirty-four. Myself, tonight, with the twelfth: not counted, as the five with the tenth were not. Thirteen.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-60.md:13:*Thirteen: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. One anomaly, the still place, read by two instruments — the tenth, which says nothing, and the twelfth, which says a shape — and understood by neither. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made. That is as far as the instruments go and I am not going past them.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-60.md:23:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-three, on the shale. The frame of the second heap, at the gap: thirty-four. The twelfth, turned on the floor at a hundred strides, on purpose: thirty-five. Myself, last night, with the twelfth: not counted. Oryn read me at the cut, asked first.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-60.md:29:*Owed, in money: nothing. Owed otherwise, and entered side by side: to Vastin, the eleventh, which came while he held a wall for us in a stair. To Teague, the thirteenth, which came at a stride while I kept his left. Neither has been told. Neither can be until the whole of it can be, and the whole of it is six people's. I used the second of them yesterday over that captain's head, on a thing that would have killed him. It does not pay the debt. A debt is not paid by something that the creditor is not let to know.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-49.md:269:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-three.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-41.md:69:"I had not counted myself. I am the worst of them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-41.md:257:*Two hundred and ninety-fourth day. Treswick; the loft, and one in the stall; the last night of both. A hundred and thirty. The back of the leaf: a list, nine lines, a thing and its number to each. Two copies, hers and the reader's, and his goes with her. The fourth line is the mark's; of its last six signs, three are sure. Fifty-two sheets counted into three boxes under two hands, K. and V. The clerk wrote* withdrawn*. Vastin: fifteen of thirty, and the stair alone. Karis wrote with the sewn hand. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-51.md:59:"Thirteenth. His. A line."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-51.md:345:*Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said* someone made this. *Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-51.md:353:*The thirteenth came at the timbers, at a stride, from Teague. It is not used. He is not told. That is the second such debt, and it is entered beside the first.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-51.md:355:*Nothing opened today: not on the shelf, and not over the iron. The read at the seep was the last. Deployment since the Line: thirty-three.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-59.md:15:*Thirty-one. Thirty-two.*

