editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:247:Pike wrote it, and said it over to the meadow, as he said everything. Forty fires had burned along that water in the dry months, with a cart or a tent to each. There were three now, and a great many black rings in the snow where the others had been; the hide-woman sat at the nearest with a skin across her knees, and she was the only person in half a mile of grass who lifted her head to hear what a crew had paid. Then his pen went down the leaf to the last line under their names, which was the season's, and stopped beside the ruled space at the end of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-01.md:281:*Hundred and thirty-third day. Lowmarch, the lower inn. The cold stay is paid: four a month, five months, twenty in front. In hand, seventy-six. The reserve is not counted here. Nine lines, and no number against the season, on purpose. Eleventh on the cloth. The board has a roof, a well-house and a fence. The fence is ours, and we go out to it on the hundred and thirty-eighth. The roof is ours as well, at five, paid when it has kept a thaw out. The mule stands in the ferryman's shed, at a fee he has not asked for and will.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-03.md:129:He walked into a shovel's haft for a quarter of an hour, in front of a bench and four pegs and whatever of the meadow had not gone back to its fires, and he was told *late* eleven times and *early* three before he had one that she did not name. She counted him as a man at a rail had once counted her, on a bluff, every morning for a month, and she was no kinder than that man had been; her right hand went on slapping the two beats long after his own legs had begun to shake.
